Fixed. All type checks pass and existing tests still pass (3 passed, 0 failed).

**The bug:** `src/import_merge.ts:7` compared URLs with a case-sensitive string equality check (`b.url === inc.url`), so two URLs differing only in hostname case (`example.com` vs `EXAMPLE.com`) were treated as distinct.

**The fix:** Added a `urlHost()` helper (src/import_merge.ts:3) that lowercases the parsed hostname — the URL spec treats hostnames case-insensitively, and `new URL()` normalizes the case for us. Matching now compares `urlHost(b.url) === urlHost(inc.url)`. Non-URL strings fall back to a plain lowercase comparison, so malformed URLs still merge when they're literally equal.

Verified: `deno check` clean, `deno test` passes. No existing tests covered `mergeImports`, so I added none — worth a dedicated test if you want regression coverage for the case-variant case.


